Acknowledgment
--------------

pybers reads and writes Apple's undocumented iWork archive format. numbers-parser
(https://github.com/masaccio/numbers-parser), by masaccio, under the MIT license, was
the first public project to reverse-engineer that format. It established that Apple
compiles the protobuf descriptors into Numbers.app, and it provided the dumper that
recovers them.

pybers includes no numbers-parser source code. Its protobuf schemas are extracted
independently from a local copy of Numbers.app by scripts/protos-extract.py, and its
object model and archive layer are separate implementations. This acknowledgment
credits the technique.
